Theorem PL-11: ContextBehavior initialization (most-optimistic seed) + componentwise join (preserves_context AND, consumes_hole AND, requires_unique_context OR, may_resume_nonlinearly OR)

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered sequence per
      Annex E §AIMS §6. PL-11 is the §07.4 TRMC
      ContextBehavior rule, governing the initialization and join of the
      ContextBehavior contract introduced by PL-7.
    - PL-11 statement (per Annex E §AIMS PL-11): the initial (most-
      optimistic) ContextBehavior is
        <preserves_context = true, consumes_hole = true,
         requires_unique_context = false, may_resume_nonlinearly = false>.
      The join is componentwise:
        preserves_context (AND), consumes_hole (AND),
        requires_unique_context (OR), may_resume_nonlinearly (OR).
    - PL-11 type signature (per Pipeline.proof lines 90-95, the sorry
      obligation this theorem discharges):
        type : List ContextBehavior -> ContextBehavior
        initial most-optimistic: <preserves_context=true, consumes_hole=true,
        requires_unique_context=false, may_resume_nonlinearly=false>;
        join: preserves_context(AND), consumes_hole(AND),
        requires_unique_context(OR), may_resume_nonlinearly(OR).
    - Shipped join: ori_arc::aims::contract::context::ContextBehavior::join
      (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/contract/context.rs lines
      70-77):
        preserves_context: self.preserves_context && other.preserves_context
        consumes_hole: self.consumes_hole && other.consumes_hole
        requires_unique_context: self.requires_unique_context || other.requires_unique_context
        may_resume_nonlinearly: self.may_resume_nonlinearly || other.may_resume_nonlinearly
      The doc comment (context.rs lines 66-68) states the direction:
      "preserves_context, consumes_hole: AND (must hold on ALL paths);
      requires_unique_context, may_resume_nonlinearly: OR (ANY path triggers)".
    - The four fields (context.rs lines 33-50): `preserves_context` (true when
      the function's return value includes the context variable — preserved on
      ALL paths), `consumes_hole` (true when the function fills the hole field
      on ALL paths), `requires_unique_context` (true when ANY path requires
      unique ownership), `may_resume_nonlinearly` (true when ANY path may resume
      more than once — derived from EffectSummary.may_share per context.rs lines
      45-49 + post_convergence.rs lines 424-431).
    - Initialization distinction (load-bearing): PL-11's "initial most-
      optimistic" seed <true, true, false, false> is the JOIN IDENTITY the
      per-region derivation folds from — joining it with any behavior yields
      that behavior unchanged. It is DISTINCT from the shipped
      ContextBehavior::default() (context.rs lines 52-63), which is the
      CONSERVATIVE contract default for functions WITHOUT TRMC candidates:
      <preserves_context = false, consumes_hole = false,
       requires_unique_context = true (conservative — require until proven
       unnecessary), may_resume_nonlinearly = false> (context.rs lines 57-60).
      The most-optimistic seed and the conservative default differ precisely
      because the former is the AND/OR join identity (optimistic per-path start)
      while the latter is the safe whole-function fallback when no derivation
      runs.
    - Derivation (per Annex E §AIMS PL-11): preserves_context true when all
      recursive calls pass the hole unchanged; consumes_hole true when all
      return paths fill the hole; requires_unique_context true when any path
      requires unique ownership; may_resume_nonlinearly true when any path may
      resume > once. The componentwise join folds the per-region behaviors with
      this AND/AND/OR/OR direction.

  Soundness property:
    Forall ContextBehavior values a, b (over the 4-tuple Bool x Bool x Bool x
    Bool domain).
      Let init = <true, true, false, false> be the most-optimistic seed and
      join(a, b) the componentwise join.
      Five conjuncts SHALL hold:

      (P1) Optimistic-initial direction:
        init.preserves_context = true AND init.consumes_hole = true
        (AND-fields seed true) AND init.requires_unique_context = false AND
        init.may_resume_nonlinearly = false (OR-fields seed false).

      (P2) Join identity:
        join(init, x) = x for every behavior x. The optimistic seed is the
        identity of the join (folding a list from init recovers the list's
        join).

      (P3) Join commutativity:
        join(a, b) = join(b, a) (componentwise AND and OR are each
        commutative).

      (P4) Join idempotence:
        join(x, x) = x.

      (P5) Join direction correctness:
        preserves_context and consumes_hole join by AND (drop to false on any
        disagreement); requires_unique_context and may_resume_nonlinearly join
        by OR (rise to true on any disagreement).

  Proof obligation:
    Five-part constructive discharge corresponding to (P1)-(P5), by
    case analysis over representative ContextBehavior values (case_analysis-led
    per the §00 PL row) + structural confirmation of the join lattice laws.

    Part (P1) — Optimistic-initial direction (structural confirmation):

      The verifier models the most-optimistic seed as
        init = <preserves_context = true, consumes_hole = true,
                requires_unique_context = false, may_resume_nonlinearly = false>
      and asserts the AND-fields seed true and the OR-fields seed false. This
      is the join identity: the top element for the AND-fields (true is the AND
      identity) and the bottom element for the OR-fields (false is the OR
      identity). A seed where an AND-field started false (would pin the joined
      result false regardless of paths) or an OR-field started true (would pin
      it true) would not be the identity — Fail. (P1) discharged.

    Part (P2) — Join identity (case analysis over representative behaviors):

      The verifier exercises join over three representative behaviors spanning
      mixed field values and asserts join(init, x) = x for each. Since AND with
      true is the identity (true && b = b) and OR with false is the identity
      (false || b = b), folding a list of per-region behaviors starting from
      init recovers exactly the componentwise join of the list. A model where
      join(init, x) != x for some x would mean init is not the identity — Fail.
      (P2) discharged.

    Part (P3) — Join commutativity (case analysis):

      The verifier asserts join(init, x) = join(x, init) over the same three
      behaviors. Componentwise AND and OR are each commutative
      (a && b = b && a; a || b = b || a), so the 4-tuple join is commutative.
      A model where the two orderings disagreed would contradict commutativity —
      Fail. (P3) discharged.

    Part (P4) — Join idempotence (case analysis):

      The verifier asserts join(x, x) = x over the three behaviors. AND and OR
      are each idempotent (a && a = a; a || a = a), so the 4-tuple join is
      idempotent. (P4) discharged.

    Part (P5) — Join direction correctness (structural confirmation on a
    concrete pair):

      The verifier joins lhs = <true, true, false, false> with rhs = <false,
      true, true, false> and asserts the result is
        <preserves_context = false (AND: true && false),
         consumes_hole = true (AND: true && true),
         requires_unique_context = true (OR: false || true),
         may_resume_nonlinearly = false (OR: false || false)>.
      This pins the AND/AND/OR/OR direction against the shipped join
      (context.rs lines 70-77). A hypothetical OR/OR/AND/AND join (the inverted
      direction) would yield a different result on this pair — Fail. (P5)
      discharged.

    Coverage gate — ContextBehavior join-case enumeration:

      The verifier discharges exactly 3 representative join cases for the
      lattice laws (require_count("PL-11", 3, ...)), plus the optimistic-initial
      direction check and the concrete direction-correctness pair. Coverage
      axes:
        Optimistic initial (P1): the <true, true, false, false> seed.
        Join identity (P2): 3 representative behaviors, join(init, x) = x.
        Commutativity (P3): join(init, x) = join(x, init).
        Idempotence (P4): join(x, x) = x.
        Direction (P5): the concrete AND/AND/OR/OR pair.

    Negative-direction witness — inverted join direction rejected:

      A join that applied OR to preserves_context / consumes_hole or AND to
      requires_unique_context / may_resume_nonlinearly would invert the
      soundness direction: a single non-context-preserving path would no longer
      force preserves_context to false, and a single unique-requiring path would
      no longer force requires_unique_context to true. The (P5) concrete-pair
      check pins the shipped AND/AND/OR/OR direction; an inverted join yields a
      different 4-tuple on lhs join rhs and Fails.

    Negative-direction witness — wrong initial seed rejected:

      Seeding the per-region fold from the CONSERVATIVE default <false, false,
      true, false> (context.rs lines 57-60) instead of the optimistic identity
      <true, true, false, false> would NOT be the join identity: joining the
      conservative default with any behavior pins preserves_context /
      consumes_hole to false (AND with false) and requires_unique_context to
      true (OR with true), corrupting the fold. The (P1) + (P2) checks pin the
      optimistic seed as the identity; using the conservative default as the
      fold seed would Fail (P2)'s join(init, x) = x.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-11 closes the TRMC cluster:

      PL-11 (ContextBehavior init + join) consumes the ContextBehavior record
      PL-7 introduces and the per-region derivation PL-8 scopes; it produces the
      joined contract field consumed by TRMC realization. Its antecedent is
      PL-7 (the 4-field record shape). PL-11 consumes no output of PL-9 / PL-10.
      The dependency chain is acyclic:
        PL-7 --> PL-11 (join over the ContextBehavior record)
      PL-11 is a sink of the TRMC-cluster dependency tree.

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      property: ContextBehavior lattice — most-optimistic
                           initialization <true, true, false, false> is the join
                           identity; the componentwise join is AND on
                           preserves_context + consumes_hole and OR on
                           requires_unique_context + may_resume_nonlinearly,
                           satisfying commutativity + idempotence + identity
      published: Leijen & Lorenzen, "Tail Recursion Modulo Context",
                           JFP 2025 (the four-field constructor-context behavior;
                           must-hold-on-all-paths vs any-path-triggers join
                           direction); standard product-lattice join discipline
                           (componentwise meet/join over a finite Boolean
                           product) per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-1..L-4
      determinism: deterministic — ContextBehavior::join is a fixed
                           componentwise Boolean expression (context.rs lines
                           70-77); no schedule or hash-order freedom; the fold
                           over per-region behaviors is permutation-invariant by
                           commutativity + associativity of AND and OR
      reference impl: ori_arc::aims::contract::context::ContextBehavior::
                           join (context.rs lines 70-77: AND on preserves_context
                           + consumes_hole, OR on requires_unique_context +
                           may_resume_nonlinearly) + the 4-field record
                           (context.rs lines 33-50) + ContextBehavior::default
                           conservative-fallback distinction (context.rs lines
                           52-63) + may_resume_nonlinearly derivation from
                           EffectSummary.may_share (context.rs lines 45-49 +
                           post_convergence.rs lines 424-431)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — confirms the optimistic-initial direction
        and the join lattice laws over the §07.4 TRMC structural model per
        section_07::verify_pl11_context_behavior_init_join; agrees with
        case_analysis on the constructive verifier)
      case_analysis (LED — per the §00 PL-row pair per the proof-checker design-proof-
        checker-design.md:102, the TRMC cluster is case_analysis-heavy; the
        verifier discharges (P1) via the seed-direction check, (P2)-(P4) via the
        three-behavior identity/commutativity/idempotence cases, and (P5) via
        the concrete AND/AND/OR/OR direction pair; constructive, NOT
        gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 case_analysis-led discharge of PL-11 via the ContextBehavior join lattice — (P1) the most-optimistic initial <preserves_context=true, consumes_hole=true, requires_unique_context=false, may_resume_nonlinearly=false> is the join identity (distinct from the conservative ContextBehavior::default per context.rs lines 52-63), (P2)-(P4) join(init, x)=x + commutativity + idempotence over three representative behaviors, and (P5) the componentwise direction is AND on preserves_context + consumes_hole, OR on requires_unique_context + may_resume_nonlinearly (context.rs lines 70-77); negative pins reject an inverted join direction and a conservative-default fold seed; structural_induction PRIMARY confirms over the same verifier
